{"module":"science","voice":"female","duration":395.6,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Science as a weapon: medicine, eugenics and reproductive control","start":0.0,"end":4.44,"words":[[0.06,0.47],[0.47,0.6],[0.6,0.74],[0.74,1.14],[1.38,1.85],[2.09,2.7],[2.7,2.9],[2.9,3.65],[3.65,4.19]]},{"el":"intro","text":"When religion could no longer justify slavery and segregation, science was asked to.","start":5.24,"end":10.59,"words":[[5.27,5.47],[5.47,6.01],[6.01,6.21],[6.21,6.41],[6.41,6.74],[6.74,7.34],[7.34,7.87],[7.87,8.07],[8.07,8.87],[9.1,9.5],[9.5,9.7],[9.7,9.97],[9.97,10.17]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This module covers what was done in medicine's name, much of it within living memory, and separates the documented record from claims that go beyond it.","start":10.94,"end":20.46,"words":[[10.99,11.2],[11.2,11.64],[11.64,12.0],[12.0,12.21],[12.21,12.43],[12.43,12.65],[12.65,12.79],[12.79,13.3],[13.3,13.66],[13.91,14.2],[14.2,14.34],[14.34,14.49],[14.49,14.85],[14.85,15.21],[15.21,15.71],[15.97,16.18],[16.18,16.83],[16.83,16.98],[16.98,17.77],[17.77,18.13],[18.13,18.42],[18.42,18.85],[18.85,19.07],[19.07,19.29],[19.29,19.72],[19.72,19.94]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Ranking humans","start":20.81,"end":22.01,"words":[[20.86,21.33],[21.33,21.87]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 1758 Carl Linnaeus divided humans into varieties and gave each a temperament: Europeans “governed by laws,” Africans “governed by caprice.”","start":22.71,"end":33.35,"words":[[22.76,22.92],[22.92,24.22],[24.22,24.45],[24.45,24.99],[24.99,25.61],[25.61,26.14],[26.14,26.45],[26.45,27.14],[27.14,27.37],[27.37,27.68],[27.68,27.91],[27.91,28.06],[28.06,28.91],[29.18,29.95],[29.95,30.41],[30.41,30.64],[30.64,30.94],[30.94,31.56],[31.56,32.02],[32.02,32.25],[32.25,32.79]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In the 1830s–40s Samuel Morton measured skull sizes to rank races, and in 1854 Josiah Nott and George Gliddon's Types of Mankind argued the races were separate species, a book widely used to defend slavery.","start":33.7,"end":49.87,"words":[[33.76,33.93],[33.93,34.1],[34.1,35.52],[35.52,36.03],[36.03,36.45],[36.45,36.87],[36.87,37.2],[37.2,37.71],[37.71,37.88],[37.88,38.21],[38.21,38.8],[39.09,39.35],[39.35,39.51],[39.51,40.52],[40.52,41.2],[41.2,41.45],[41.45,41.7],[41.7,42.12],[42.12,42.71],[42.71,43.13],[43.13,43.3],[43.3,43.97],[43.97,44.39],[44.39,44.56],[44.56,45.06],[45.06,45.23],[45.23,45.73],[45.73,46.32],[46.61,46.78],[46.78,47.03],[47.03,47.54],[47.54,47.87],[47.87,48.04],[48.04,48.55],[48.55,49.3]]},{"el":"s0","text":"None of it holds up: modern genetics finds more variation within any so-called race than between them.","start":50.22,"end":56.51,"words":[[50.27,50.48],[50.48,50.62],[50.62,50.75],[50.75,51.16],[51.16,51.37],[51.61,51.95],[51.95,52.57],[52.57,52.98],[52.98,53.12],[53.12,53.88],[53.88,54.22],[54.22,54.43],[54.43,54.91],[54.91,55.18],[55.18,55.39],[55.39,55.8],[55.8,56.07]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Experiments without consent","start":57.41,"end":59.28,"words":[[57.47,58.28],[58.28,58.69],[58.69,59.16]]},{"el":"s1","text":"J.","start":59.98,"end":60.62,"words":[[60.02,60.26]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Marion Sims, 1845–1849: the “father of modern gynecology” developed his surgery by operating repeatedly, without anesthesia, on enslaved women including Anarcha, Betsey and Lucy.","start":60.97,"end":75.09,"words":[[61.02,61.47],[61.47,61.85],[62.11,64.29],[64.55,64.7],[64.7,65.0],[65.0,65.16],[65.16,65.53],[65.53,66.43],[66.43,67.03],[67.03,67.26],[67.26,67.79],[67.79,68.01],[68.01,68.69],[68.69,69.44],[69.7,70.15],[70.15,70.9],[71.17,71.32],[71.32,71.92],[71.92,72.29],[72.29,72.89],[72.89,73.35],[73.61,73.98],[73.98,74.21],[74.21,74.59]]},{"el":"s1","text":"New York City removed his Central Park statue in 2018.","start":75.44,"end":79.86,"words":[[75.49,75.72],[75.72,75.96],[75.96,76.26],[76.26,76.73],[76.73,76.96],[76.96,77.5],[77.5,77.74],[77.74,78.2],[78.2,78.36],[78.36,79.36]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Tuskegee, 1932–1972: the U.S. Public Health Service followed about 600 Black men in Alabama, 399 of them with syphilis, without telling them their diagnosis and without treating them, even after penicillin became the standard cure in the 1940s.","start":80.21,"end":100.11,"words":[[80.21,80.88],[81.14,83.5],[83.76,83.91],[83.91,84.28],[84.65,85.09],[85.09,85.39],[85.39,85.76],[85.76,86.2],[86.2,86.57],[86.57,87.38],[87.38,87.68],[87.68,87.9],[87.9,88.05],[88.05,88.64],[88.9,90.53],[90.53,90.67],[90.67,90.9],[90.9,91.12],[91.12,91.71],[91.97,92.41],[92.41,92.78],[92.78,93.0],[93.0,93.22],[93.22,94.04],[94.04,94.26],[94.26,94.7],[94.7,95.15],[95.15,95.44],[95.7,96.0],[96.0,96.29],[96.29,96.96],[96.96,97.4],[97.4,97.55],[97.55,98.07],[98.07,98.36],[98.36,98.51],[98.51,98.66],[98.66,99.62]]},{"el":"s1","text":"It ended only when a whistleblower went to the press.","start":100.46,"end":103.68,"words":[[100.51,100.65],[100.65,100.98],[100.98,101.31],[101.31,101.51],[101.51,101.64],[101.64,102.31],[102.31,102.58],[102.58,102.71],[102.71,102.84],[102.84,103.17]]},{"el":"s1","text":"President Clinton apologized in 1997.","start":104.03,"end":108.03,"words":[[104.09,104.74],[104.74,105.25],[105.25,106.04],[106.04,106.19],[106.19,107.56]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Henrietta Lacks, 1951: cells taken from her cancer without her knowledge became the HeLa line used in labs worldwide.","start":108.38,"end":116.4,"words":[[108.43,109.07],[109.07,109.42],[109.66,110.79],[111.03,111.31],[111.31,111.73],[111.73,112.01],[112.01,112.16],[112.16,112.51],[112.51,112.93],[112.93,113.07],[113.07,113.49],[113.49,113.91],[113.91,114.05],[114.05,114.33],[114.33,114.61],[114.61,114.89],[114.89,115.03],[115.03,115.31],[115.31,115.95]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Her family reached a settlement with one company in 2023.","start":116.75,"end":120.57,"words":[[116.8,116.92],[116.92,117.28],[117.28,117.58],[117.58,117.7],[117.7,118.25],[118.25,118.43],[118.43,118.61],[118.61,119.04],[119.04,119.16],[119.16,120.12]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Eugenics and forced sterilization","start":121.47,"end":124.3,"words":[[121.51,122.3],[122.3,122.56],[122.56,122.92],[122.92,124.15]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In Buck v. Bell (1927) the Supreme Court upheld forced sterilization (“Three generations of imbeciles are enough”).","start":125.0,"end":133.62,"words":[[125.05,125.2],[125.2,125.44],[125.44,125.67],[126.06,126.3],[126.3,127.7],[127.98,128.13],[128.13,128.6],[128.6,128.83],[128.83,129.3],[129.3,129.62],[129.62,130.71],[130.71,130.94],[130.94,131.88],[131.88,132.04],[132.04,132.66],[132.66,132.74],[132.74,133.13]]},{"el":"s2","text":"It has never been overruled.","start":133.97,"end":135.59,"words":[[134.02,134.14],[134.14,134.31],[134.31,134.54],[134.54,134.71],[134.71,135.22]]},{"el":"s2","text":"More than 60,000 people were sterilized under laws in 32 states.","start":135.94,"end":141.3,"words":[[135.99,136.15],[136.15,136.4],[136.4,137.49],[137.49,137.91],[137.91,138.07],[138.07,138.91],[138.91,139.24],[139.24,139.49],[139.49,139.66],[139.66,140.16],[140.16,140.74]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Early victims were mostly poor white people labeled “feebleminded”; after the 1950s, in the South especially, they were increasingly Black women.","start":141.65,"end":150.93,"words":[[141.69,141.9],[141.9,142.4],[142.4,142.54],[142.54,143.04],[143.04,143.25],[143.25,143.54],[143.54,143.89],[143.89,144.39],[144.39,145.31],[145.56,145.84],[145.84,145.99],[145.99,146.98],[147.23,147.37],[147.37,147.51],[147.51,147.79],[147.79,148.43],[148.68,148.89],[148.89,149.04],[149.04,149.75],[149.75,150.03],[150.03,150.46]]},{"el":"s2","text":"North Carolina's Eugenics Board sterilized about 7,600 people from 1929 to 1974.","start":151.28,"end":159.83,"words":[[151.33,151.55],[151.55,152.29],[152.29,152.95],[152.95,153.17],[153.17,153.91],[153.91,154.27],[154.27,155.97],[155.97,156.34],[156.34,156.63],[156.63,157.88],[157.88,158.03],[158.03,159.28]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In 2013 it became the first state to pay survivors.","start":160.18,"end":163.82,"words":[[160.23,160.37],[160.37,161.11],[161.11,161.25],[161.25,161.65],[161.65,161.79],[161.79,162.06],[162.06,162.39],[162.39,162.53],[162.53,162.73],[162.73,163.34]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Fannie Lou Hamer was sterilized without consent in 1961 while having a tumor removed.","start":164.17,"end":170.23,"words":[[164.2,164.49],[164.49,164.63],[164.63,164.99],[164.99,165.2],[165.2,165.92],[165.92,166.35],[166.35,166.85],[166.85,167.0],[167.0,168.15],[168.15,168.43],[168.43,168.79],[168.79,168.94],[168.94,169.29],[169.29,169.8]]},{"el":"s2","text":"She called it a “Mississippi appendectomy,” a common experience among Black women in the South.","start":170.58,"end":176.55,"words":[[170.58,170.73],[170.73,171.04],[171.04,171.2],[171.2,171.35],[171.35,171.97],[171.97,172.89],[172.89,173.05],[173.05,173.43],[173.43,174.36],[174.36,174.66],[174.66,174.97],[174.97,175.36],[175.36,175.51],[175.51,175.67],[175.67,176.05]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The Relf sisters, ages 12 and 14, were sterilized at a federally funded clinic in Montgomery, Alabama, in 1973.","start":176.9,"end":187.35,"words":[[176.96,177.12],[177.12,177.43],[177.43,177.99],[178.27,178.75],[178.75,179.15],[179.15,179.39],[179.39,179.86],[180.14,180.3],[180.3,181.1],[181.1,181.26],[181.26,181.42],[181.42,182.06],[182.06,182.53],[182.53,183.01],[183.01,183.17],[183.17,184.05],[184.33,184.96],[185.24,185.4],[185.4,186.83]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Their lawsuit led to federal consent rules.","start":187.7,"end":190.61,"words":[[187.74,187.96],[187.96,188.32],[188.32,188.54],[188.54,188.69],[188.69,189.2],[189.2,189.72],[189.72,190.08]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Native women: a 1976 federal audit (GAO) found 3,406 sterilizations by the Indian Health Service in just four of its twelve areas from 1973 to 1976, many with inadequate consent.","start":190.96,"end":208.9,"words":[[191.02,191.51],[191.51,192.0],[192.29,192.45],[192.45,193.92],[193.92,194.49],[194.49,194.82],[194.82,195.07],[195.35,195.76],[195.76,197.8],[197.8,199.03],[199.03,199.28],[199.28,199.44],[199.44,199.93],[199.93,200.26],[200.26,200.67],[200.67,200.83],[200.83,201.24],[201.24,201.4],[201.4,201.56],[201.56,201.81],[201.81,202.22],[202.22,202.71],[202.71,203.04],[203.04,204.43],[204.43,204.59],[204.59,206.14],[206.43,206.76],[206.76,207.0],[207.0,207.74],[207.74,208.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Puerto Rico: by 1965 about a third of mothers had been sterilized, under programs encouraged by U.S. and island officials.","start":209.25,"end":218.09,"words":[[209.3,209.76],[209.76,210.15],[210.38,210.58],[210.58,211.7],[211.7,212.03],[212.03,212.16],[212.16,212.36],[212.36,212.49],[212.49,212.82],[212.82,213.02],[213.02,213.21],[213.21,213.94],[214.17,214.43],[214.43,215.02],[215.02,215.61],[215.61,215.81],[215.81,216.14],[216.47,216.67],[216.67,217.06],[217.06,217.59]]},{"el":"s2","text":"California sterilized about 20,000 people from 1909 to 1979, and nearly 150 women in state prisons from 2006 to 2010; a 2014 state audit found consent rules were broken.","start":218.44,"end":234.77,"words":[[218.44,219.13],[219.13,219.89],[219.89,220.27],[220.27,221.25],[221.25,221.63],[221.63,221.93],[221.93,222.92],[222.92,223.07],[223.07,224.51],[224.78,225.01],[225.01,225.39],[225.39,226.68],[226.68,227.06],[227.06,227.21],[227.21,227.59],[227.59,228.12],[228.12,228.42],[228.42,229.41],[229.41,229.56],[229.56,230.32],[230.59,230.74],[230.74,231.57],[231.57,231.95],[231.95,232.25],[232.25,232.63],[232.63,233.17],[233.17,233.47],[233.47,233.62],[233.62,234.23]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Immigration detention: a 2022 bipartisan U.S. Senate investigation found that women at the Irwin County center in Georgia underwent excessive and often unnecessary gynecological procedures.","start":235.12,"end":248.48,"words":[[235.18,235.91],[235.91,236.57],[236.83,236.97],[236.97,238.0],[238.0,238.73],[238.73,239.1],[239.46,239.83],[239.83,240.78],[240.78,241.15],[241.15,241.37],[241.37,241.74],[241.74,241.88],[241.88,242.03],[242.03,242.32],[242.32,242.76],[242.76,243.13],[243.13,243.27],[243.27,243.71],[243.71,244.3],[244.3,244.81],[244.81,245.03],[245.03,245.33],[245.33,246.06],[246.06,247.16],[247.16,247.89]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Margaret Sanger and the “Negro Project”","start":249.38,"end":251.96,"words":[[249.43,249.89],[249.89,250.36],[250.36,250.59],[250.59,250.74],[250.74,251.21],[251.21,251.83]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Margaret Sanger founded the American Birth Control League in 1921, which became Planned Parenthood in 1942.","start":252.66,"end":261.11,"words":[[252.71,253.15],[253.15,253.6],[253.6,254.12],[254.12,254.27],[254.27,254.86],[254.86,255.09],[255.09,255.68],[255.68,255.91],[255.91,256.05],[256.05,257.32],[257.58,257.88],[257.88,258.32],[258.32,258.69],[258.69,259.44],[259.44,259.59],[259.59,260.63]]},{"el":"s3","text":"She supported eugenics, as many Progressive-era reformers did, and spoke to a women's auxiliary of the Ku Klux Klan in 1926.","start":261.46,"end":270.97,"words":[[261.46,261.61],[261.61,262.14],[262.14,262.9],[263.17,263.32],[263.32,263.63],[263.63,264.61],[264.61,265.15],[265.15,265.45],[265.72,265.94],[265.94,266.32],[266.32,266.48],[266.48,266.63],[266.63,267.08],[267.08,267.77],[267.77,267.92],[267.92,268.07],[268.07,268.22],[268.22,268.6],[268.6,268.91],[268.91,269.06],[269.06,270.43]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In 2020 Planned Parenthood of Greater New York removed her name from its Manhattan clinic over her eugenics ties.","start":271.32,"end":277.83,"words":[[271.37,271.49],[271.49,272.24],[272.24,272.55],[272.55,273.16],[273.16,273.29],[273.29,273.66],[273.66,273.85],[273.85,274.03],[274.03,274.4],[274.4,274.53],[274.53,274.78],[274.78,275.02],[275.02,275.21],[275.21,275.7],[275.7,276.08],[276.08,276.32],[276.32,276.45],[276.45,277.01],[277.01,277.31]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In 1939 her federation started the “Negro Project” to bring birth control to the rural South.","start":278.18,"end":285.16,"words":[[278.22,278.37],[278.37,279.51],[279.51,279.67],[279.67,280.42],[280.42,280.88],[280.88,281.03],[281.03,281.49],[281.49,282.1],[282.1,282.25],[282.25,282.55],[282.55,282.78],[282.78,283.39],[283.39,283.54],[283.54,283.69],[283.69,284.15],[284.15,284.53]]},{"el":"s3","text":"W.E.B. Du Bois and Mary McLeod Bethune supported it.","start":285.51,"end":289.99,"words":[[285.56,286.37],[286.74,286.88],[286.88,287.18],[287.18,287.4],[287.4,287.77],[287.77,288.28],[288.28,288.73],[288.73,289.24],[289.24,289.46]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In a letter about it, Sanger wrote: “We do not want word to go out that we want to exterminate the Negro population, and the minister is the man who can straighten out that idea if it ever occurs to any of their more rebellious members.”","start":290.34,"end":302.58,"words":[[290.39,290.52],[290.52,290.65],[290.65,290.9],[290.9,291.22],[291.22,291.42],[291.64,292.03],[292.03,292.35],[292.57,292.7],[292.7,292.83],[292.83,293.02],[293.02,293.28],[293.28,293.47],[293.47,293.6],[293.6,293.79],[293.79,293.98],[293.98,294.17],[294.17,294.3],[294.3,294.56],[294.56,294.69],[294.69,295.39],[295.39,295.52],[295.52,295.91],[295.91,296.67],[296.9,297.09],[297.09,297.22],[297.22,297.67],[297.67,297.8],[297.8,297.93],[297.93,298.12],[298.12,298.25],[298.25,298.44],[298.44,298.95],[298.95,299.14],[299.14,299.34],[299.34,299.66],[299.66,299.78],[299.78,299.91],[299.91,300.11],[300.11,300.36],[300.36,300.49],[300.49,300.68],[300.68,300.81],[300.81,301.0],[301.0,301.13],[301.13,301.64],[301.64,302.09]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Historians disagree about that sentence.","start":302.93,"end":305.52,"words":[[302.97,303.61],[303.61,304.06],[304.06,304.38],[304.38,304.57],[304.57,305.08]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Most read it as worry that rumors would sink the project, not as a secret plan; critics read it as revealing.","start":305.87,"end":313.08,"words":[[305.92,306.29],[306.29,306.52],[306.52,306.67],[306.67,306.82],[306.82,307.12],[307.12,307.34],[307.34,307.72],[307.72,307.94],[307.94,308.24],[308.24,308.39],[308.39,309.07],[309.33,309.56],[309.56,309.71],[309.71,309.86],[309.86,310.31],[310.31,310.68],[310.94,311.47],[311.47,311.7],[311.7,311.85],[311.85,312.0],[312.0,312.6]]},{"el":"h4","text":"“Planned Parenthood was founded to exterminate Black Americans”","start":313.98,"end":317.72,"words":[[314.02,314.37],[314.37,315.06],[315.06,315.27],[315.27,315.76],[315.76,315.9],[315.9,316.67],[316.67,316.95],[316.95,317.58]]},{"el":"s4","text":"This claim, common in political campaigns, goes beyond the record.","start":318.42,"end":322.78,"words":[[318.47,318.66],[318.66,319.05],[319.28,319.61],[319.61,319.74],[319.74,320.32],[320.32,320.91],[321.14,321.4],[321.4,321.79],[321.79,321.92],[321.92,322.31]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Sanger opposed abortion in her lifetime; she promoted contraception.","start":323.13,"end":327.55,"words":[[323.18,323.58],[323.58,323.99],[323.99,324.39],[324.39,324.52],[324.52,324.66],[324.66,325.26],[325.5,325.63],[325.63,326.23],[326.23,327.11]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Planned Parenthood did not provide abortions until about 1970.","start":327.9,"end":332.45,"words":[[327.92,328.26],[328.26,328.93],[328.93,329.14],[329.14,329.34],[329.34,329.81],[329.81,330.28],[330.28,330.62],[330.62,330.96],[330.96,331.97]]},{"el":"s4","text":"The documented coercion against Black, Native and Latina women came mainly from state eugenics boards and government-funded programs, not from a hidden plan inside one organization.","start":332.8,"end":344.44,"words":[[332.85,333.0],[333.0,333.77],[333.77,334.26],[334.26,334.68],[334.68,335.03],[335.27,335.69],[335.69,335.9],[335.9,336.32],[336.32,336.67],[336.67,336.95],[336.95,337.38],[337.38,337.66],[337.66,338.01],[338.01,338.64],[338.64,338.92],[338.92,339.13],[339.13,340.18],[340.18,340.88],[341.13,341.34],[341.34,341.62],[341.62,341.76],[341.76,342.11],[342.11,342.39],[342.39,342.81],[342.81,343.02],[343.02,343.93]]},{"el":"s4","text":"This site takes no position on abortion.","start":344.79,"end":347.24,"words":[[344.85,345.04],[345.04,345.29],[345.29,345.61],[345.61,345.8],[345.8,346.24],[346.24,346.36],[346.36,346.81]]},{"el":"s4","text":"It documents coercion: anyone, on any side, who wants to end it should know where it actually happened.","start":347.59,"end":353.92,"words":[[347.66,347.79],[347.79,348.45],[348.45,348.98],[349.21,349.67],[349.9,350.03],[350.03,350.23],[350.23,350.56],[350.79,350.93],[350.93,351.26],[351.26,351.39],[351.39,351.59],[351.59,351.72],[351.72,351.92],[351.92,352.11],[352.11,352.31],[352.31,352.44],[352.44,352.97],[352.97,353.43]]},{"el":"h5","text":"What the numbers show today","start":354.82,"end":356.49,"words":[[354.87,355.1],[355.1,355.26],[355.26,355.73],[355.73,355.96],[355.96,356.35]]},{"el":"s5","text":"CDC abortion surveillance reports show the abortion rate among Black women is roughly four times the rate among white women.","start":357.19,"end":364.68,"words":[[357.21,357.68],[357.68,358.15],[358.15,358.86],[358.86,359.33],[359.33,359.56],[359.56,359.72],[359.72,360.19],[360.19,360.51],[360.51,360.82],[360.82,361.13],[361.13,361.53],[361.53,361.68],[361.68,362.08],[362.08,362.23],[362.23,362.63],[362.63,362.78],[362.78,363.1],[363.1,363.41],[363.41,363.73],[363.73,364.2]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Research from the CDC and the Guttmacher Institute links this to higher rates of unintended pregnancy, which in turn follow from unequal access to contraception and health care, from poverty, and from well-earned distrust of the medical system.","start":365.03,"end":381.2,"words":[[365.08,365.55],[365.55,365.87],[365.87,366.03],[366.03,366.51],[366.51,366.75],[366.75,366.91],[366.91,367.47],[367.47,368.19],[368.19,368.59],[368.59,368.82],[368.82,368.98],[368.98,369.3],[369.3,369.7],[369.7,369.86],[369.86,370.66],[370.66,371.46],[371.74,372.06],[372.06,372.21],[372.21,372.45],[372.45,372.85],[372.85,373.17],[373.17,373.73],[373.73,374.13],[374.13,374.29],[374.29,375.25],[375.25,375.49],[375.49,375.8],[375.8,376.12],[376.4,376.72],[376.72,377.28],[377.56,377.8],[377.8,378.12],[378.12,378.6],[378.6,379.23],[379.23,379.39],[379.39,379.55],[379.55,380.11],[380.11,380.67]]},{"el":"s5","text":"The same unequal system shows up elsewhere: Black women die from pregnancy-related causes at about two and a half to three times the rate of white women (CDC), a gap that holds even for college-educated women.","start":381.55,"end":394.74,"words":[[381.6,381.75],[381.75,382.04],[382.04,382.57],[382.57,383.01],[383.01,383.31],[383.31,383.46],[383.46,383.98],[384.24,384.54],[384.54,384.91],[384.91,385.13],[385.13,385.43],[385.43,386.69],[386.69,387.07],[387.07,387.22],[387.22,387.59],[387.59,387.74],[387.74,387.96],[387.96,388.11],[388.11,388.33],[388.33,388.48],[388.48,388.7],[388.7,389.08],[389.08,389.22],[389.22,389.52],[389.52,389.67],[389.67,389.97],[389.97,390.34],[390.34,390.86],[391.12,391.27],[391.27,391.49],[391.49,391.72],[391.72,392.16],[392.16,392.46],[392.46,392.61],[392.61,393.8],[393.8,394.25]]}]}